{"name":"Stoplight","hex":"#dd1111","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stoplight","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A traffic control signal, traditionally consisting of three lights, colored green, yellow/amber, and red, meaning proceed, prepare to stop, and stop, respectively.","A light on the rear of a vehicle that is activated when braking; a brake light."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stoplight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Traffic light","blocks":[{"text":"Traffic lights, traffic signals, or stoplights – also known as robots in South Africa, Zambia, and Namibia – are signalling devices positioned at road intersections, pedestrian crossings, and other locations to control the flow of traffic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Modern_British_LED_Traffic_Light.jpg/330px-Modern_British_LED_Traffic_Light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Traffic_light"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Traffic_lights.jpg/500px-Traffic_lights.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Traffic_lights.jpg/1280px-Traffic_lights.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Traffic_lights.jpg/500px-Traffic_lights.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Traffic lights can have several additional lights for filter turns or bus lanes.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATraffic_lights.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Japanese_signal_aokibashi.jpg/500px-Japanese_signal_aokibashi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Jap